cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use defog-megan, please cite it (the paper reference is added here when it is public), and cite the DeFoG paper it builds on."
title: "defog-megan: Generating Graphs for a Reason – Explanation-Conditioned Adapters for Discrete Flow Matching"
type: software
abstract: "Code and trained models for concept-conditioned graph generation. A frozen DeFoG discrete flow-matching generator is steered by a property adapter and a concept adapter, with the concept condition taken from the membership vector of a self-explaining GNN (MEGAN). The package also has Feynman-Kac steering, the scorers and the experiments of the paper, and a model zoo."
keywords:
  - graph generation
  - discrete flow matching
  - conditional generation
  - explainable AI
  - concept explanations
  - adapters
  - molecular generation
  - pytorch
